      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Find $f_{y}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=e^{3 x + 3 y}+x^{3} y^{4}$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Differentiate with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as constant. First write $e^{3 x + 3 y}=e^{3 x}\\cdot e^{3 y}$ to expose the held exponential factor. Apply the sum and constant multiple rules term by term.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(e^{3 x + 3 y}) &=e^{3 x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(e^{3 y}) \\\\\n&=e^{3 x}\\cdot \\left(3 e^{3 y}\\right) \\\\\n&=3 e^{3 x + 3 y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x^{3} y^{4}) &=x^{3}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y^{4}) \\\\\n&=x^{3}\\cdot \\left(4 y^{3}\\right) \\\\\n&=4 x^{3} y^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $f_{y}(x,y)=4 x^{3} y^{3} + 3 e^{3 x + 3 y}$.",
